{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Ephraim has become</b> — in its lightness and lack of sense, that they would go to Egypt and Assyria to seek help, and they did not know that when they go I will spread My net over them, and I will catch them, for they cannot flee. Therefore he said about them and not to them. And because he mentioned a dove, he said: like a bird of the sky I will bring them down."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:30.118930940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}